bring in chad wolfe former acting  homeland security secretary to talk more  about this  um first of all let's just talk about  the immigration  crisis as a whole john saki actually  won't even address it as an actual  crisis  nancy pelosi calls it a humanitarian  crisis it seems that they just can't get  their vocab  to mesh but never mind what you call it  it doesn't matter the point is  it is indeed a crisis and kamala harris  where is she she's supposed to be  looking at the root cause of it right  that's what she was  that was the job she was given so where  is kamala harris in all this  well you're absolutely right and whether  you called a crisis or a challenge  the reality is we are seeing historic  numbers on that southwest border  of the legal apprehensions of minors of  families most of those being released  into the u.s  it's overwhelming the border patrol it's  overwhelming dhs and it's overwhelming  local communities so  any way you cut it there's a crisis  going on at the border it doesn't seem  to be ending any time in sight  because we know the biden administration  right now is not pursuing  any policies that will stem the flow of  these individuals coming into the  country and of course you showed that  video  of those two uh young girls being thrown  over  a border fence that is the direct result  of  this administration advertising that it  is okay  that they will continue to allow minors  to stay in the country if they arrive at  the border it is an inhumane policy and  we are seeing the results of that  i mean the video is just horrifying  i mean the the two little girl toddlers  are  plopped down onto our side of the border  there is the agent who rescued these two  little girls now they have no family  and they are now going to join the some  5767 children  uh in customs and border patrol uh con  custody as of just this past sunday and  those numbers  are skyrocketing in fact cnn is  reporting that the us is on track to  record  two million migrants on the southern  border by the end of the year  what is the plan to make it stop forget  the  the the focus on the root of the cause  how about just  the solution that's just it  again i've said that the administration  continues to address this issue as  though it's a capacity issue  trying to bring on more facilities and  uh  facilitating the introduction of these  individuals into the country  and that is the wrong approach you've  got to address the illegal behavior  that's happening at that border  to stop the flow to stop the the tide  uh that is coming in and the surge that  is coming in so that's really where they  need to be focused it's not where  they're focused today  so i urge them to change course in doing  that but again you talked about  the miners there's over 5000 about 5 000  in custody cbp custody another 7 or 8  000 in hhs custody and for dhs  that's almost double what we saw in the  height of the crisis in 2019 when  so many on the far left and others were  so outraged at what was going on in the  border they have doubled the amount of  minors in cbp facilities today  and then again it's a direct result of  these policies that they have been  pursuing since inauguration day there  are ways to fix this  right and border patrol and dhs can stun  the tide very very quickly  chad i want to talk to you about another  growing crisis and uh it's a new fox  news uh analysis  which shows that crime surging in  democrat-led cities  that slashed police funding last year  this is an issue murders  up 46 percent in minneapolis 271 percent  in portland oregon  12 percent here in new york city 28 in  los angeles  and in los angeles county more  controversy around new district attorney  george  gascon who critics call pro-criminal  sources reportedly saying that he's  planning to downsize  and rename the city's hardcore gang unit  the sister of a man killed by a gang  member  speaking here this morning watch i just  can't believe that he's actually making  this action  it was actually the work of the gang  unit and the hardcore  gang unit in the da's office that really  kind of pull this case together  it is really unfortunate because these  gangs in la streets are very very real  and they're very very dangerous  quite often which is in the case of my  brother innocent people are caught in  the crossfire of  this gang activity i mean this is no  surprise an uptick in crime when  different democratic-led counties are  reducing their  budgets for police i mean what did they  expect was going to happen that all the  criminals were going to go into hiding  well this is exactly what we talked  about last summer when this big push to  defund the police  and really to look closely at police  procedures what we did in the trump  administration is we came out with a set  of reform  principles that we could we believe that  the law enforcement community could back  and they did  but what we saw from the left again is  going very much beyond that and going to  defund the police  take down gang units and and other  measures and we see the dramatic  and detrimental effects that that is  having and we see places like  minneapolis  and portland that have now trying to  retract some of the  measures that they took over the summer  uh but it's it's certainly not working  and some of these big cities  that have this approach whether it's  seattle minneapolis portland or  there's three or four others um they're  going in the wrong direction they're  going in the wrong direction and  and they need to take a playbook out of  those other large cities  uh that have made uh police reform  not only prosperous in the sense of  making sure that you're bringing in more  resources you're providing the  leadership and the training  to police here's what i wanted in a very  productive way i want to know what the  where the biden administration stands in  all of this because you remember there  was sort of a back and forth about  whether  joe biden during the election um  supported to fund the police  movement or didn't um and he did come  forward finally after a lot of pressure  because he was silent on it for quite  some time  and said that he did not support to fund  the police but he however thought that  each city or each county needed to deal  with it on its own but  at what point does the biden  administration stand up and tell these  counties look  this is not the time to be slashing  budgets  if there has ever been a time to get  behind the men and women in blue  protecting our country and our innocent  civilians the time is now  well you're exactly right the president  has largest microphone  out there when he speaks uh or  members of his administration speak some  folks do listen and so they need to come  out they need to support the men and  women in blue  they need to back law enforcement  because at the end of the day  these are the individuals that put their  lives on the line to protect our  communities  big and small and they need to have the  backing of their commander-in-chief they  need to have the backing of the  president  and every day and every week that he's  silent he doesn't talk about this and we  see  you know news in portland they are still  targeting federal facilities and federal  agents in portland today  and again the administration is silent  on that it seems as though they only  want to talk about the events of january  6th right  here in d.c but if there's a violence  towards other federal officers or  facilities  they don't want to talk about it i  always say silence speaks volumes chad  wolf thank you very much for talking to  us

